        "section": "8 / Detailed Mechanisms of Ion Fragmentation"
      },
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "curator_note": "Eq 8.5, lower scheme, alpha-alpha channel (arrow labelled 'aa'). Radical-driven McLafferty-type rearrangement of the n-butyl vinyl ether molecular ion: the terminal-vinyl odd electron abstracts the gamma-H, the resulting C-radical drives C-O cleavage, and the C2H4O acetaldehyde fragment retains charge+radical (keto acetaldehyde, IE=10.2 eV printed; higher IE than butene so only 20%). Book draws 4 fishhook arcs (terminal-C gamma-H abstraction; C4=C5 pi formation; C-O cleavage); moves 1,4,6 correspond to those, moves 2,3,5 are the implicit partner homolysis/pairing hooks (not drawn). Precursor written as the distonic oxa-allyl resonance form .CH2-CH=O(+)- (odd electron on the terminal carbon as drawn); acetaldehyde radical cation localized with +. on oxygen. m/z curator-computed; 20% printed. [RECHECK 2026-07-24: arc count corrected 3->4 per a zoomed re-read; the gamma-H abstraction is drawn as TWO barbs (O-radical->H and the gamma C-H bond electron->O-H), not one.]"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "ev_mech",
      "source_id": "mod_rules",
