        "figure": null,
        "panel": null,
        "section": null
      },
      "confidence": 0.4,
      "curator_note": "Cross-link: M\u00d8D rule IMS_8_5_2. Same caveat as the alpha-i record: skeleton matches (gamma-H transfer, C-O cleavage, alkene + carbonyl) but the rule is over-valent (ether O valence 4, adjacent C valence 5; reactant C6H15O) and non-conserving (products +2 / 2 radicals vs +1/1), hence chemically invalid and guardrail-dropped. IMS_8_5_2 localizes the charge on the butene, i.e. the alpha-i (not this alpha-alpha) outcome."
    }
